MID_SE_Tal_Fia_C: <EDH>
MID_SE_Tal_Fia_C_001: What a day... Those soldiers came charging at me\nlike they wanted to die.
MID_SE_Tal_Fia_C_002: Welcome back, Talimun. I'm glad to see you\nappear unhurt.
MID_SE_Tal_Fia_C_003: Fianna?! How'd you get in my quarters? The door\nwas locked, wasn't it?
MID_SE_Tal_Fia_C_004: I've been here since you left. I used a copy of the key\nto open the door, and I've been keeping watch here.
MID_SE_Tal_Fia_C_005: You made a copy? You can see why that concerns\nme as chief executive of the company, can't you?
MID_SE_Tal_Fia_C_006: "Concerns"? Why?
MID_SE_Tal_Fia_C_007: One's quarters are...sacred, you see—where one can\ngo to clear his mind without worry of prying eyes...
MID_SE_Tal_Fia_C_008: And here you are, having taken it upon yourself\nto enter uninvited? I return it to you... Why?
MID_SE_Tal_Fia_C_009: When I'm with you, I'm able to relax. I wanted to\nunderstand why.
MID_SE_Tal_Fia_C_010: Since I lost my memory, strangers—especially men—\nhave made me uneasy.
MID_SE_Tal_Fia_C_011: I see... I wonder if that has something to do with\nthe repressed memories of your incident.
MID_SE_Tal_Fia_C_012: I just can't shake the thought that we must have met\nbefore! It's the only way I can explain these feelings.
MID_SE_Tal_Fia_C_013: We've definitely never met. I always remember\na pretty face, so I'd know.
MID_SE_Tal_Fia_C_014: Think about it. How could I forget a beauty like\nthis, huh?
MID_SE_Tal_Fia_C_015: Oh...
MID_SE_Tal_Fia_C_016: What about Centurio? He's a man, and you got\nalong with him alright, didn't you?
MID_SE_Tal_Fia_C_017: He cared for me for four years. I gave him quite\na bit of trouble in the beginning, I assure you.
MID_SE_Tal_Fia_C_018: With how intimidating he is, everything inside me\nscreams to run and hide at the sight of him.
MID_SE_Tal_Fia_C_019: I can't imagine you'd get very far with him on your\ntail, eh?
MID_SE_Tal_Fia_C_020: Ahem... You are not wrong.
MID_SE_Tal_Fia_C_021: I'd scream for him to get away from me, in the\nmiddle of the street, in front of everyone...
MID_SE_Tal_Fia_C_022: I'm sure the bystanders thought the chief celestial\ngeneral of the vulkans was bullying some girl.
MID_SE_Tal_Fia_C_023: I imagine so. Once I got used to our situation, I tried\nto make it up to him with tea and other favors.
MID_SE_Tal_Fia_C_024: I'm glad Centurio didn't have to fight you the whole\ntime—and even got a little something for the effort.
MID_SE_Tal_Fia_B: <EDH>
MID_SE_Tal_Fia_B_001: Damn. Talk about barbarity... I look away for half\na second, and this is what happens.
MID_SE_Tal_Fia_B_002: Pardon my interruption, but...is everything alright?
MID_SE_Tal_Fia_B_003: Oh, we just lost a caravan full of goods to thieves.\nNothing I haven't seen in all my years, but...
MID_SE_Tal_Fia_B_004: After a few centuries, the repetitiveness of it all\nloses some appeal.
MID_SE_Tal_Fia_B_005: To suffer for so long, you poor thing... How about\nI make you some of my special tea?
MID_SE_Tal_Fia_B_006: When I served it to Centurio, he'd always find the\nwill to work like a man possessed.
MID_SE_Tal_Fia_B_007: "A man possessed"? But he was already so devoted\nto his work...
MID_SE_Tal_Fia_B_008: Yes. He was. If you'd like to try some, I will go\nprepare a pot now.
MID_SE_Tal_Fia_B_009: Your tea is served.
MID_SE_Tal_Fia_B_010: This tea smells familiar... I think our company trades\nin this variety.
MID_SE_Tal_Fia_B_031: Though, there's another scent I'm getting...\nHas something been added to it?
MID_SE_Tal_Fia_B_032: Yes. I take a soothing tea, mix in some rare spices,\nand steep it for three days and nights.
MID_SE_Tal_Fia_B_033: Then I add water to the concentrate, so it's not quite\nso strong—and honey as a sweetener.
MID_SE_Tal_Fia_B_034: After Centurio drank it, he slept for nearly two\nfull days.
MID_SE_Tal_Fia_B_035: Ahaha... I understand now why he'd redouble his\nefforts at work after losing two days.
MID_SE_Tal_Fia_B_036: And he only drank the tea once, I imagine?
MID_SE_Tal_Fia_B_037: Th-that's right... I did offer it to him from time\nto time, but he always declined...
MID_SE_Tal_Fia_B_038: I wanted for him to be able to forget his worries\nand relax, if only for a little while.
MID_SE_Tal_Fia_B_039: I'm sure he appreciated your good intentions.\nThat's probably why he drank it in the first place.
MID_SE_Tal_Fia_B_040: I'm thankful as well, of course. It's just that I care\nwhat happens to me, you see.
MID_SE_Tal_Fia_B_041: I care about what happens to you too!
MID_SE_Tal_Fia_B_042: Then will you treat me as I would treat myself?\nEven if it means I don't drink your tea?
MID_SE_Tal_Fia_B_043: It's true there's plenty of unpleasantness in this life.\nThere's always some damn thing...
MID_SE_Tal_Fia_B_044: But still, I choose to face life head-on, no matter\nwhat comes. Because I care what happens.
MID_SE_Tal_Fia_B_045: I understand. You are under no obligation to try\nthe tea.
MID_SE_Tal_Fia_B_046: Well, I suppose after you went to all the trouble of\nbrewing it, I should at least taste it, shouldn't I?
MID_SE_Tal_Fia_B_047: Are you sure? It won't interfere with your work?
MID_SE_Tal_Fia_B_048: Centurio slept for two days, right? As a demigod,\nI imagine I'll be out a day at most.
MID_SE_Tal_Fia_B_049: A single day of lost work will be easy enough to\ncatch up on... If I have you to help me, that is.
MID_SE_Tal_Fia_B_050: I'd love to help however I'm able!
MID_SE_Tal_Fia_B_051: Well, alright then. Let's see now... Hey, this\nis pretty good. This...is...
MID_SE_Tal_Fia_B_052: Hehehe. You look so lovely as you sleep, Talimun...
